Your Interview Readiness Test

By December, you should be able to sit for an interview and handle:

Round 1: DSA — 1–2 medium problems

Round 2: Java + Spring Boot + SQL

Round 3: Backend/LLD/System Design

Round 4: Project + Managerial/Behavioral

The biggest mistake would be spending September–December endlessly watching courses. Every learning day should produce something measurable: a solved problem, a piece of code, an interview answer, a project feature, or a mock interview.

For a 1-year Java backend engineer, depth beats technology collection. Master Java + Spring Boot + SQL + DSA first, then demonstrate Redis/Kafka/system-design knowledge around a project.
